; epi_merge.simi — M2.15: epilogue/prologue merging across a single-edge
; BACKWARD fold, LIVE-executed. The fold at pc 9 targets pc 4 (r4 = 4, an
; EARLIER pc — a backward fold), and pc 4 is reached ONLY via that fold
; (pc 3's BR targets the FOLD SOURCE at pc 6, not pc 4 — no fall-through
; into the head, no BR/BC/CALL, no other JMPR, no entry edge). The head
; block's first instruction (pc 4) reads r2, r1 — the reload pattern. The
; source block's tail (pc 8) reads the SAME r2, r1 in the SAME order — the
; same register-frame reload pattern, emitted a few words earlier. The
; tail's fetches leave r2 in x9 and r1 in x10 (transient — the cache
; directory only holds the RESULTS r4/r5/r9, so the fold's flush at pc 9
; stores x11 only and does NOT touch x9/x10). When control lands at pc 4,
; x9 still holds r2 and x10 still holds r1: the head's reloads would
; re-read the same slot values into the same hosts — dead. The merge
; DROPS them, so the frame is loaded once (at the tail), not once per
; block. The layout is rigid (pattern@T, RET@T+1, two LOADIs@T+2/T+3,
; matching tail@T+4, fold@T+5) and the pre-T result registers (r2, r1)
; are pairwise distinct, so the cache cursor at the tail is exactly the
; result count mod 3 (= 2), the tail's result lands in x11, and BOTH head
; fetches drop (2 words). A teeth check that reverts the merge grows the
; file back by exactly 8 bytes.
;
; The head's pattern writes r0 = r2 + r1, so the expected result (7)
; flows THROUGH the dropped reads: the three interpreter engines compute
; it from the SIMI semantics, and the ARM engine executes the emitted
; code — a wrong drop (say a cursor error yielding wrong flags) makes the
; ARM result differ from the interpreters and the four-way parity fails
; on its own. This is what makes the test self-validating rather than a
; dead-path shape verified only by dump inspection.
; Expected result: 7
.entry main
main:
    ENTER #8
    LOADI r2, #3, i64        ; pc 1 — the pattern's first source (r2 = 3)
    LOADI r1, #4, i64        ; pc 2 — the pattern's second source (r1 = 4)
    BR src                   ; pc 3 — T-1: terminal, jumps INTO the fold source
target:                      ; pc 4 = T — reached only via the fold at pc 9
    ADD r0, r2, r1, i64      ; pc 4 — the pattern: reads r2, r1 (reloads) — r0 = 7
    RET                      ; pc 5 — returns r0 = 3 + 4 = 7
src:                         ; pc 6 — the fold source (the BR target)
    LOADI r4, #4, i64        ; pc 6 — fold index (r4 = 4, folds BACKWARD to pc 4)
    LOADI r5, #9, i64        ; pc 7 — second dead-region result
    ADD r9, r2, r1, i64      ; pc 8 — the tail: reads r2, r1 (same pattern)
    JMPR r4                  ; pc 9 — folds to pc 4 — the single incoming edge
